&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Skeletons, lasers, tattoo buses — the Torq brand grabs attention like nothing else in cybersecurity. And we&#39;re growing like crazy, backed by Series D funding, 200% employee growth, and 300% revenue growth. Fueling Torq&#39;s momentum is our game-changing AI SOC platform, backed by a team and culture that makes Torq one of Forbes&#39; Best Startup Employers in America, and a Business Insider &#39;startup to bet your career on&#39;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life at Torq is all gas, no brakes. We&#39;re a team of relentless, collaborative go-getters pushing the boundaries of what&#39;s possible for security automation. Every role is an essential driver of Torq&#39;s success as the AI-native autonomous SecOps platform of choice for security teams across the Fortune 500.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;jobDetailsDescriptionGroup jobDetailsDescriptionGroup--expanded jobDetailsDescriptionGroup-enter-done&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;jobDetailsDescriptionGroupColumn&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;jobDetailsDescriptionText jobDetailsDescriptionText--expanded&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;BambooRichText&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own Torq&#39;s Builder Experience domain - a core part of how security teams design, build, and deploy automations. As AI fundamentally changes how security operations work, this role sits at the center of that shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires genuine product craft - the ability to see what security teams actually struggle with and shape tools that feel intuitive and powerful - alongside frontier AI product thinking: defining how a conversational AI should behave, where its limits are, how it earns trust, and how it sharpens with every interaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end builder experience - from understanding where security teams get stuck to shipping flows that feel intuitive and powerful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care about how the product looks and feels. Partner closely with Design to turn ambiguity into clear, usable flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive our conversational AI product forward as a first-class part of the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how we evaluate the AI experience: define what &quot;good&quot; means, how we measure quality, and how we improve it continuously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform customer research and hands-on deep-dives to understand how people build and where they get stuck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze usage patterns and feedback to spot signal and translate it into actionable engineering requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make critical decisions on trade-offs across experience, capability, and technical design to meet business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering to define, develop, and launch new capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our company and team spirit foster an environment that encourages taking initiative, being open to new ideas, and enjoying the ride!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Ideal Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience as a product manager on SaaS products, OR 2+ years in PM following an engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense for UX and UI. You understand user pain and can shape an experience that fits it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in AI products. You&#39;re curious about how they behave, how they fail, and how they earn user trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical fluency to work closely with engineering and reason about how the product is built and consumed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven, with the ability to ask the right questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal skills, able to drive teams and interfaces without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication. You can move between a customer conversation, a design review, and an engineering spec without dropping the thread&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Science degree or equivalent technical background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI/LLM products or agent-based interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating and improving product quality with metrics and experimentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in security, DevOps, or automation platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering tightly with Design on visual, interaction-rich products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal-opportunity employer, we are committed to a team defined and empowered by diversity. We consider qualified applicants without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are waiting for you!&lt;/p&gt;
